<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Cóndor Pasa (Los Incas)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental version, later the base track of Simon &amp; Garfunkel's recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Cóndor Pasa (If I Could) (Simon &amp; Garfunkel)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1970</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new English words by Paul Simon</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Cóndor Pasa (Perry Como, on It's Impossible)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1970</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover of Simon's version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Cóndor Pasa (Julie Felix)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1970</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover of Simon's version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Cóndor Pasa (James Last Orchestra)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1970</span><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Cóndor Pasa (Armando Robles Godoy)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new Spanish words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El Cóndor Pasa (Eduardo Falú)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement for solo guitar</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Spirit of the Hawk (Leo Rojas)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">flute and pan flute version</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Traditional Andean folk music of Peru</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the melody</span></li></ul></section>
